From 1c641a0137d6a0c9cd9886463db892863d4e02e6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: [REDACTED] <redacted>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 02:08:43 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] fix(setup): classify setup model by total RAM so 8 GB devices
 get a model

recommend_setup_model required ram_gb_min + 2 GiB of FREE RAM for the 4B
model, so an 8 GB laptop (~7.7 GiB total) always got model_id=None.

- Add guenther/model_budgets.py as the single RAM budget source for
  device_check.py and setup_models.py. Budgets are minimum required GiB
  per class (higher is stricter); 27B uses the stricter 14.0.
- 4B is recommended from 7.0 GiB total. low_free_ram is set when free
  RAM is below a reachable per-class threshold (4B: 3.3e9-byte i3 peak
  gate in GiB + 0.5 GiB, ~3.57 GiB; 8B/27B: class budget).
- 8B fits / is an alternative from 15.0 GiB total. The 8B recommendation
  gate stays at 23 GiB total and 4 cores and additionally needs a peak
  attestation; fewer than 4 physical cores sets slow_cpu.
- 27B thresholds are unchanged (47 GiB total, 12 physical cores).
- model_id is None only with reason ram_too_small or disk_too_small.
- SetupRecommendation gains reason, warnings, alternatives, fits and
  per-model peak_unverified, all with defaults. fits is a device check on
  installed RAM: class gate, and for 8B/27B class budget + 2 GiB <= total
  (27B never fits 16 GB devices), plus disk. alternatives = other fitting
  models.
- PEAK_ATTESTATION keeps every model unverified until a complete
  physical-i3 record exists: commit, measurement_sha256, device,
  model_sha256 matching the catalog artifact, peak_private_bytes and
  peak_bytes <= 3.3e9, Job Object method, ship_evidence, not hard_fail.
- device_check applies the same class gates; 27B variants and the 8B
  Q2_K candidate are floored by the shared class minimum.

Tests prove the logic only; the i3 / 8 GB peak gate stays open.
The setup panel is unchanged; it does not yet list the recommended 4B
on an 8 GB device (strict xfail, needs a Designer adapter).
